<urn:aspace:05-from-v2-domains-30-business-os-00-jerry-business-pulse-04-business-domains-00-links-20-life-os-para-portal-01-projects-picard-00-agency-as-a-service-b2-business-domains-08-legal-aquaman-eternals-05-aaas-legal-transverse-risk-boundary-os-md> a aspace:Document ;
    rdfs:label "AAAS Legal Transverse Risk Boundary OS  ## Purpose Legal is the transverse risk gate for 00 Agency as a Service. It ensures claims, data, IP, compliance, contracts, authority, liability, and approval boundaries are explicit before B2/B3 work becomes public or operational.  ## Operating Thesis AaaS needs Legal to keep client claims, data handling, IP ownership, service terms, and contractor/client boundaries explicit before delivery scales.  ## Eight-Domain Legal Interface | Domain | Legal Surface | Required Proof | | --- | --- | --- |" ;
    aspace:seau <urn:aspace:05-from-v2-domains> ;
    dct:modified "2026-06-02" ;
    aspace:mots 270 .

<urn:aspace:05-from-v2-domains-30-business-os-00-jerry-business-pulse-04-business-domains-00-links-20-life-os-para-portal-01-projects-picard-00-agency-as-a-service-b2-business-domains-08-legal-aquaman-eternals-06-aaas-b2-b3-legal-review-protocol-md> a aspace:Document ;
    rdfs:label "AAAS B2/B3 Legal Review Protocol  ## Legal Packet Every B2/B3 task that touches a claim, contract, client/member/entity/childcare/field data, IP, billing/refund/tax responsibility, public message, or authority boundary must carry this packet:  project: 00 Agency as a Service b2_domain: b2_owner: b3_agent: legal_surface: claim_or_commitment: data_or_record_path: ip_or_deliverable_boundary: terms_or_contract_boundary: liability_or_safety_boundary: authority_owner: review_needed: proof_required: decision:  ## Assignment Rules | Rule | Standard | | --- | --- | | One legal surface | The risk category is explicit | | One authority owner | Approval and responsibility are named | | One proof path | Decision evidence is attached | | One escalation | Uncertain work routes to Legal/B1/Donna | | One boundary | Allowed, conditional, blocked, or external review |  ## Refusal Conditions Legal blocks execution when: - public claims are unsupported; - data path or privacy boundary is unclear; - IP or deliverable ownership is vague; - terms, waiver, refund, tax, or liability boundary is missing; - authority to decide/sign/commit is unclear; - external professional review is needed but absent.  ## Output Legal emits one of three states: - LEGAL_READY: B3 can execute inside the named boundary. - NEEDS_REVIEW: work returns to Legal/B2 for clarification. - BLOCKED_RISK: work routes to Donna/DLQ or B1." ;
    aspace:seau <urn:aspace:05-from-v2-domains> ;
    dct:modified "2026-06-02" ;
    aspace:mots 160 .

